{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122598","id":4314900984,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABATAp-A","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122598","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122598.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122598.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122598","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122598/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122598/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122598/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/b7dc79ac722ffbe0cc7d55b4c1c9d0087742a80a","number":122598,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[Core] Add `get_method_info` to Callable","user":{"login":"og-mrk","id":70659536,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNjU5NTM2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70659536?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/og-mrk","html_url":"https://github.com/og-mrk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/og-mrk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/og-mrk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/og-mrk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/og-mrk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/og-mrk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/og-mrk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/og-mrk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/og-mrk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/og-mrk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/10969\r\n- Works toward adding runtime checks for Callable-Signal upon connecting (see https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14266 for more info)\r\n  Please note this's not best solution, as we could statically check, which'll be better, but adding runtime checks is better then having no checks at all.\r\n\r\n<details><summary><h2>Interested for a spin? (Testing changes out)</h2></summary>\r\n<p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you're a user of the Engine, or experienced with code base, you can test these changes by:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n\r\n<li>Downloading the CI builds (<a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/37212232316/artifacts/11307324266\">Windows</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/37212232316/artifacts/11307996104\">MacOS</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/37212232316/artifacts/11308305862\">Linux</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/37212232316/artifacts/11307930326\">Android</a>)\r\n</li>\r\n\r\n<li>having any <code>Callable</code> in your script, and calling <code>.get_method_info()</code>, which returns a Dictionary representing the method (see <a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a3088fecf1837aa22fcf2bccae413598a2e91766/core/object/method_info.h#L48\">struct def</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a3088fecf1837aa22fcf2bccae413598a2e91766/core/object/method_info.cpp#L37-L51\">Dictionary convertion</a> for more info). returned Dictionary contains following keys:\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><code>name</code>: name of method (of type <code>String</code>)</li>\r\n    <li><code>args</code>: an array of dictionaries, each one represents an argument (which's a Dictionary representing <b>PropertyInfo type</b>, see below)</li>\r\n    <li><code>default_args</code>: an array of variants representing default values of optional arguments.</li>\r\n    <li><code>flags</code>: a integer representing what the method is (see <a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a3088fecf1837aa22fcf2bccae413598a2e91766/core/object/method_info.h#L36\">MethodFlags enum</a>)</li>\r\n    <li><code>id</code>: unique identifier (of type <code>int</code>)</li>\r\n    <li><code>return</code>: what the method returns (Dictionary representing <b>PropertyInfo type</b>, see below)</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</li>\r\n\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<b>PropertyInfo as Dictionary:</b>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><code>name</code>: name of the argument, which's a <code>String</code></li>\r\n<li><code>class_name</code>: name of argument's class, which's a <code>StringName</code></li>\r\n<li><code>type</code>: type of argument, which's a <code>Variant::Type</code>, as an <code>int</code> (Enum value), <a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/94a23991c683254d8b5ef63f4f5e017b995c4c2f/core/variant/variant.h#L97\">enum definition here</a></li>\r\n<li><code>hint</code>: a hint useful to know what this argument is, as an <code>int</code> (Enum value), <a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a3088fecf1837aa22fcf2bccae413598a2e91766/core/object/property_info.h#L39\">enum definition here</a></li>\r\n<li><code>hint_string</code>: string representation of <code>hint</code></li>\r\n<li><code>usage</code>: a useful hint on what to do with this argument, as an <code>int</code> (Enum value), <a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a3088fecf1837aa22fcf2bccae413598a2e91766/core/object/property_info.h#L88\">enum definition here</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n</p>\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<details><summary><h2>Use of AI</h2></summary>\r\n<p>\r\n\r\n<p>I've used AI only in specific instances, of which are:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>better understand C#/GD script interop, as somethings weren't clear to me, this allowed me to test implement of <code>get_method_info()</code> in <code>ManagedCallable</code>, it didn't tell straight away on how to trigger it, used my knowledge from reading godot docs about C#/GD Interop and asked it to write a simple example, which I've read through and changed a lot to fit my needs.</br>\r\nAI model used was Google's Gemini AI, specific model version is unknown to me, as I've asked it few weeks ago, and I'm unfamiliar with AI as a whole.. so idk how to extract model number.. apologies for my ignorance 😓</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n</details>","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":709269775,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MDkyNjk3NzU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:dotnet","name":"topic:dotnet","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","follow